  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Science Programme, ISP, 2014-2019 - International Science Programme ISP 2014-2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">International Science Programme, ISP, 2014-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Scientific research and postgraduate education in basic sciences (Chemistry, Maths and Physics) is strengthened in low-income countries and the research results are used to address development problems.
2. Better planning of, and improved conditions for, carrying out research and postgraduate training.
3. Increased production of high quality research results.
4. Increased use of research results and graduates
5. High quality applications are awarded funds by ISP.
6. Suitable conditions for carrying out research are created.
7. Maintained or increased production of PhDs by ISP supported research
groups and networks.
8. Maintained or increased number of quality publications.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Genom International Science Programme, ISP, vid Uppsala Universitet,  st&#xf6;der Sida forskargrupper och n&#xe4;tverk i l&#xe5;ginkomstl&#xe4;nder inom        basvetenskaper (matematik, fysik och kemi). St&#xf6;det avser utveckling   av forskning, MSc och PhD-utbildning samt anv&#xe4;nds f&#xf6;r anskaffning av  utrustning, litteratur, etc.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the International Science Program, ISP, coordinated at        Uppsala University, Sida supports research groups and networks in     low-income countries in basic sciences (mathematics, physics and      chemistry). The support is given for research development, MSc and    PhD education, acquisition of equipment, literature etc.</narrative>
  </description>
